From: Zak Peirce <zak@orbis-win>
Subject: profile: accept [runtime] version so a generator can declare one

runtime_field returned PW_ERR_UNSUPPORTED for every key it did not know, and
"version" was one of them, so a profile carrying it was refused whole.

Playden gates its "32-bit code" setting -- cpu = native|translator, which this
parser has read all along -- on the kit claiming the profile-version-2
capability, and a kit that claims it writes "version = 2" into [runtime]
alongside the cpu line. So the capability could not be declared: declaring it
would have made every generated profile unparseable here. Not declaring it
leaves the setting greyed out as "Needs a newer runtime kit", which is why an
imported game was stuck on native and MDK -- a 1997 32-bit title that needs the
translator -- crashed five seconds in with c0000005 at a 32-bit address
(2026-11-18).

The key names the profile's generation and selects nothing by itself: every
key is read the same way whatever it says. So accept 1 and 2, once, and ignore
it. Bit 16 of runtime_seen was free; 1, 2, 4 and 8 are thread_scheduling, cpu,
shared_input and fast_clock, and the 16 at line 268 belongs to display_seen,
a separate mask.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

--- a/src/pw_game_profile.c
+++ b/src/pw_game_profile.c
@@ -398,7 +398,7 @@ static int debug_field(PwGameProfile *profile, const uint8_t *key, size_t key_le
     return PW_OK;
 }
 
-/* [runtime] thread_scheduling, shared_input, fast_clock: true/false or
+/* [runtime] version: 1 or 2; thread_scheduling, shared_input, fast_clock: true/false or
  * 1/0; cpu: native or translator; each once. */
 static int runtime_field(PwGameRuntime *runtime, uint32_t *seen, const uint8_t *key, size_t key_length,
                          const uint8_t *v, size_t n)
@@ -414,6 +414,19 @@ static int runtime_field(PwGameRuntime *runtime, uint32_t *seen, const uint8_t *
         *seen |= 2u;
         return PW_OK;
     }
+    /* [runtime] version = 1|2 names the profile's generation. The runtime reads every key it
+     * supports whatever the generation says, so the value only has to be one we know; it selects
+     * nothing by itself. Accepting it is what lets a generator declare version 2 -- Playden gates
+     * its "32-bit code" setting (cpu = native|translator, read above) on the kit claiming
+     * profile-version-2, and writes "version = 2" alongside it. Without this that line came back
+     * PW_ERR_UNSUPPORTED and the whole profile was refused, so the setting could not be offered at
+     * all and an imported game was stuck on native. */
+    if (is(key, key_length, "version")) {
+        if (*seen & 16u) return PW_ERR_MALFORMED;
+        if (!is(v, n, "1") && !is(v, n, "2")) return PW_ERR_UNSUPPORTED;
+        *seen |= 16u;
+        return PW_OK;
+    }
     if (is(key, key_length, "thread_scheduling")) bit = 1u, field = &runtime->thread_scheduling;
     else if (is(key, key_length, "shared_input")) bit = 4u, field = &runtime->shared_input;
     else if (is(key, key_length, "fast_clock")) bit = 8u, field = &runtime->fast_clock;
